Adaptations:
- Separate 6.18 PID/IPC, procfs, task exit, allocation, fork and IPC backend implementations.
- Retain native release_task_post, pidmap seqcount lock and per-namespace pid_max.
- Use ns_common references/initialization and native namespace trees; register initial PID/IPC
  namespace roots only once all activation patches have succeeded.
- Shared host state stays external; missing SysV task fields use a lifecycle-managed side table.
- Disable duplicate boot initcalls and provide explicit backend init/exit with deferred cleanup.
- Restore namespace references for perf, BPF task iterator, cgroup-v1 pidlist and FUSE.
- Preserve the native FUSE io_uring teardown and connection initialization fields.
- Handle PID/IPC pidfd namespace ioctls and forward other pidfd commands to the native body.
- Validate KCFI signatures, callback targets and original prologues before patching.
- Keep BTI landing instructions and native KCFI prefixes; original trampolines return with a
  range-checked direct branch, preserving PAC/SCS and avoiding indirect branches mid-function.
- Replace native ARM64 syscall slots under stop_machine; no 32-bit IPC implementation.
- SHM_HUGETLB rejected with EOPNOTSUPP; native memfd allocation and sealing retained.
- Module activation is pinned until reboot. GKI family opt-in and userspace ABI checks are required.
